	<section class="mb-24 w-full prose dark:prose-invert" style="width:100%; max-width:800px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
		<div class="prose-content w-full" style="width:100%;">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">Mastering Date Math: How to Calculate Days Between Dates</h2>
			<p style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				Whether you're planning a project sprint, tracking contract deadlines, calculating legal notice periods, or simply curious about a milestone—like finding out "<strong>how many days have I lived?</strong>"—knowing the exact <strong>number of days between dates</strong> is an essential daily need. While simple date subtraction sounds straightforward, factors like leap years, varying month lengths, and working schedules can introduce unexpected calculation errors. Our <strong>days between dates calculator</strong> handles all calendar math instantly with 100% precision.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">How to Calculate Days Between Dates: Step-by-Step</h3>
			<p style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				Calculating the duration between any two dates on our calculator takes just four quick steps:
			</p>
			<ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				<li><strong>Select your Start Date:</strong> Enter or pick the starting point of your interval.</li>
				<li><strong>Select your End Date:</strong> Choose your target milestone, deadline, or past event date.</li>
				<li><strong>Choose End Date Inclusion:</strong> By default, the calculator measures the elapsed duration (excluding the last day). Check <em>"Include end date (add 1 day)"</em> if both the first and last day represent full active days.</li>
				<li><strong>Click "Calculate Days":</strong> Instantly view the total calendar days, working business days, full weeks, approximate months, and total percentage of a year.</li>
			</ol>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">How Leap Years Affect Date Calculations</h3>
			<p style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				A standard calendar year has 365 days, but an astronomical solar year is approximately 365.2422 days long. To keep our calendar aligned with Earth's orbit around the sun, the Gregorian calendar adds an extra leap day—<strong>February 29th</strong>—every four years (years divisible by 4, except century years unless also divisible by 400, such as 2000).
			</p>
			<p style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				When calculating durations manually or using simple formulas (like multiplying years by 365), failing to account for leap days produces an off-by-one error. Our calculator uses standardized UTC calendar normalization to automatically count every February 29 that falls within your specified date range.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">Counting Business Days vs. Calendar Days</h3>
			<p style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				In project management, billing, and employment contracts, raw calendar days are often not enough. You frequently need to know <strong>how many business days between two dates</strong>. Our calculator automatically filters out Saturdays and Sundays, giving you the exact count of Monday-through-Friday working days to help you plan project timelines and delivery schedules with confidence.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">Excel Formulas vs. Online Date Calculator</h3>
			<p style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				In spreadsheet tools like Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets, finding date differences usually requires formulas such as <code>=DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, "d")</code> or <code>=NETWORKDAYS(start_date, end_date)</code> for working days. While effective, spreadsheets require manual setup and formula memorization. CountDays gives you the same mathematical precision on any browser or mobile device with zero setup.
			</p>

			<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">Common Use Cases</h3>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2" style="width:100%; max-width:800px;">
				<li><strong>Project & Sprint Planning:</strong> Estimating working days available between sprint kick-off and delivery.</li>
				<li><strong>Legal & Financial Deadlines:</strong> Tracking statutory notice windows, loan interest accruals, or contract expiration dates.</li>
				<li><strong>Life Milestones:</strong> Celebrating your 10,000th day alive with our <a href="#life-tools" class="text-link hover:underline">Days Lived</a> counter.</li>
				<li><strong>Event Countdowns:</strong> Finding exact days remaining until holidays, weddings, exams, or vacations.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

